<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46049" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subsessor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				waylayer</i>, <i>lier-in-wait</i> (post-Aug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subsessores vocantur, qui occisuri aliquem
					delitescunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A. 11, 268</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 498</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subsessores cum venabulis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 40, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">alieni matrimonii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 2, 1, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">7, 2</span></i>, ext. 1;
			cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subsessoris et adulteri persona,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 4, p. 142</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
